From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:41:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: sg-pc the phone's buttons do not also hide the text

Backing out of phone screens with the Back button toggled the engine's hide-text (UI hidden) at the same time, so
after the phone closed the message could not be advanced any more until hidden again (seen after the PhoneWave call
of SG01_12: three backs -> text hidden -> taps ignored). New UI::GameSpecific::SceneInputTaken(): for STEINS;GATE
true while flag 2610 says the player drives the phone; UpdateGameState does not toggle the hide state then.

Checked on MuMu (Android 15, not a real device, original English data): SG01_12 from the save at Daru's loop,
by taps only: small phone -> mail -> back x3 -> address book -> PhoneWave -> call -> text advances -> dial 120#
-> the story continues into the next scenes.

TYN only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

